<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI11-QA7-ARCH-001-HARDCODED-ALLOWLIST>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI11-QA7-ARCH-001-HARDCODED-ALLOWLIST" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-Legacy ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-22T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:title "Deletion gate AST scan uses a hardcoded 5-file allowlist instead of a full workspace sweep" ;
  triage:description "In fn ai11_deletion_gate_rejects_retired_windows_transport_ast_and_dependencies() (crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs, commit bb20fd9a on feature/pAI-s11-post-merge-remediation, PR #607), the `guarded_sources` array hardcodes exactly 5 files (protocol.rs, atm-daemon/src/lib.rs, local_tcp_transport.rs, atm-daemon-client/src/lib.rs, atm/src/composition.rs) and only scans those via retired_windows_transport_ast_findings(). Two sibling guards in the SAME file already do a full workspace-wide sweep instead of a fixed allowlist: fn production_code_cannot_restore_retired_error_contract_symbols() and fn workspace_source_must_not_reintroduce_retired_peer_delivery_constructs() (also fn only_the_error_contract_module_may_define_an_atm_error_literal()), all of which call collect_rust_files(&workspace_root().join(\"crates\"), &mut files) and scan every workspace Rust file. The narrower 5-file allowlist means any new file added anywhere else in the workspace that reintroduces retired Windows pipe/AF_UNIX/frame-codec constructs would NOT be caught by this gate. No active production violation exists today -- the risk is purely the gate's ability to catch a FUTURE regression. arch-qa (ARCH-001) and ruthless-boundary-qa (RBQA-F001) both independently found this same root cause during QA-7. Fix: widen `guarded_sources` to a full collect_rust_files workspace sweep, following the exact pattern already used by the two sibling guards in this file." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "boundary-gate-weakness" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed_partial" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-22T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI11-QA7-ARCH-001-HARDCODED-ALLOWLIST/pAI-s11/1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAI-s11/bb20fd9a> ;
  triage:fixedOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAI-s12/b6466aa1> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAI-s11/bb20fd9a> ;
  triage:highestOpenBranch "feature/pAI-s11-post-merge-remediation" ;
  triage:highestFixedBranch "feature/pAI-s12-post-write-router" ;
  triage:references "PR #607: https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/607#issuecomment-5050812060" ;
  triage:references "commit bb20fd9a" ;
  triage:notes "QA-7 fast-follow on top of AI11-QA5-ATM-QA-002-DELETION-GATE-TEST.ttl, which is already closed as fixed citing bb20fd9a and must NOT be reopened or touched. Do not modify that finding's ttl file." ;
  triage:correctionNote "quality-mgr (2026-07-26): independent re-verification per team-lead directive on task #1177, not trusting the existing occurrence closureNote. Confirmed directly against crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs at integrate/phase-AI head: fn ai11_deletion_gate_rejects_retired_windows_transport_ast_and_dependencies (L1343) now calls ai11_guarded_workspace_sources(&root) (L1358), which is defined at L1663 and performs collect_rust_files(&root.join(\"crates\"), &mut files) -- a genuine full-workspace recursive sweep, not the old 5-file guarded_sources allowlist. grep confirms no remaining `guarded_sources` array literal anywhere in the file; the sibling helper is also reused at L1438 for a second guard, matching the pattern the original finding asked for. Existing closureNote's disposition is CONFIRMED correct. No edits needed beyond this confirmation." .

<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI11-QA7-ARCH-001-HARDCODED-ALLOWLIST>
  triage:assignedTo "cwin" ;
  triage:dispatchChannel "direct-paste-non-atm" ;
  triage:notes "ASSIGNMENT UPDATE (team-lead, 2026-07-22): the AI.11 QA-7 fast-follow batch (this finding plus AI11-QA7-ATM-QA-201-ENVELOPE-CODEC-COVERAGE and AI11-QA7-ARCH-002-TAUTOLOGICAL-DUPLICATE-CHECK) was reassigned from arch-ctm to cwin. Original ATM dispatch was message 01KY5PZ9PCJMZP3ZFA92NGCGS5 (task id AI11-QA7-FASTFOLLOW-DELETION-GATE-SCOPE, sent to arch-ctm). arch-ctm was subsequently stood down from this batch via ATM message 01KY5S0ZFQCPA89KD5WTM0Z6CA. cwin has no ATM identity, so the reassignment dispatch to cwin was delivered by direct-paste outside the ATM channel and left no ATM message trail on cwin's side; the stand-down message to arch-ctm is the only ATM-side record of the handoff. This note is the canonical audit trail for the reassignment." .

